---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import FareTable from '../components/FareTable.astro';
import { destinations, fleet } from '../lib/fleet';

const site = 'https://adelaideairporttobarossa.com.au';
const slug = 'adelaide-airport-to-angaston-transfer';
const url = `${site}/${slug}`;

const d = destinations.angaston;
const tan = destinations.tanunda;
const [sedan, tarago, hiace] = fleet;

/* Township-specific questions only. The generic distance and duration questions are
   owned in schema by the logistics page, so three URLs do not compete for one query. */
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How long is the transfer from Adelaide Airport to Angaston?',
    a: `About ${d.min} minutes door to door, roughly ${d.km} km. Angaston is the furthest of the central Barossa townships, on the valley's eastern edge.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How much is a transfer from Adelaide Airport to Angaston?',
    a: `$${sedan.now} flat per car for up to ${sedan.seats} passengers, each way, the same as Tanunda. $${tarago.now} for the seven-seat people mover and $${hiace.now} for the thirteen-seat bus.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you go past Angaston to Eden Valley or Keyneton?',
    a: 'Yes, but those are outside the central townships the flat fare covers. Give us the address when you book and the fare comes back in writing before you fly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you pick me up in Angaston for a flight home?',
    a: 'Yes, at the same flat fare, timed back from your departure. Allow a little more time than from Tanunda, since Angaston is the longest run to the airport.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Adelaide Airport to Angaston transfers',
    serviceType: 'Private airport transfer',
    description: `Private chauffeur transfer between Adelaide Airport and Angaston, about ${d.km} km and ${d.min} minutes. Flat fare per vehicle, each way.`,
    provider: { '@id': `${site}/#business` },
    areaServed: { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Angaston, South Australia' },
    url,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
    })),
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${site}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Adelaide Airport to Angaston', item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Content
  title="Adelaide Airport to Angaston Transfer | $200 Flat, 70 Minutes"
  description="Private transfer from Adelaide Airport to Angaston. $200 flat per car, about 80 km and 70 minutes, the same fare as Tanunda. Flight tracked, met in arrivals."
  slug={slug}
  h1="Adelaide Airport to Angaston transfers"
  eyebrow="Angaston &middot; the Barossa's eastern edge"
  lead={`Angaston is about ${d.km} km from Adelaide Airport, roughly ${d.min} minutes by road. A private transfer is $${sedan.now} flat per car for up to ${sedan.seats} passengers, each way, the same fare as the closer townships.`}
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <p><strong>Angaston is the furthest of the central Barossa townships</strong>, and the one where a
  flat fare works hardest for you. It is about {d.km - tan.km} km past Tanunda, and the price does
  not move.</p>

  <h2>Why people stay in Angaston</h2>

  <p><strong>It is the quieter, older end of the valley.</strong> Angaston sits on the eastern edge
  of the Barossa, where the valley floor starts to rise toward the Eden Valley ranges. Stone
  buildings, a short main street and fewer tour buses than Tanunda.</p>

  <p><strong>Yalumba is here.</strong> Samuel Smith founded it near Angaston in 1849, and it is
  still family owned. For a lot of visitors it is the reason Angaston is on the itinerary at all.</p>

  <p><strong>Saturday mornings belong to the Barossa Farmers Market</strong>, held in the Vintners
  Sheds on the corner of Stockwell and Angaston Roads. If you land on a Friday, that is a good
  reason to book a Friday-night transfer and wake up already here.</p>

  <h2>The drive: the long way, at the same price</h2>

  <p>Out of the airport, north around the city on the <strong>Northern Expressway, past
  Gawler</strong>, then onto the Sturt Highway. Through the valley floor past Nuriootpa, then east
  into Angaston.</p>

  <p><strong>About {d.km} km, about {d.min} minutes</strong>, door to door in normal traffic. That
  is roughly ten minutes longer than Tanunda. The flat fare covers the central townships without
  grading them by distance, so the extra ten minutes cost you nothing.</p>

  <h2>The Angaston fare is the Tanunda fare</h2>

  <p><strong>Ten more minutes on the road, nothing more on the price.</strong> The fare is set per
  vehicle for the whole central valley, so the furthest township costs what the middle one does.</p>

  <FareTable caption="Per vehicle, each way, Angaston included." />

  <p><strong>A delayed landing is the driver's problem, not yours.</strong> The pick-up follows your
  flight number, and on a run this long that matters: nobody wants to start a seventy-minute drive
  worrying about a missed connection.</p>

  <p><a class="btn" href="/#book">Get your Angaston transfer &rarr;</a></p>

  <h2>Staying past Angaston?</h2>

  <p><strong>Eden Valley, Keyneton and the properties up in the ranges are outside the central
  area</strong> the flat fare covers. They are still a normal booking: give us the address, and the
  fare comes back in writing before you fly rather than as a surprise on arrival.</p>

  <p><strong>Not set on Angaston yet?</strong> Tanunda puts you in the middle of the valley, about
  ten minutes closer to the airport, at the same fare.</p>

  <p><a href="/adelaide-airport-to-tanunda-transfer">Adelaide Airport to Tanunda transfers
  &rarr;</a></p>

  <h2>Angaston transfer questions</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    {faqs.map((f) => (
      <>
        <h3>{f.q}</h3>
        <p>{f.a}</p>
      </>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>Flying home from Angaston?
  <a href="/barossa-to-adelaide-airport-transfer">Barossa to Adelaide Airport</a> &middot;
  More than four of you?
  <a href="/group-transfers-adelaide-airport-barossa-valley">Group transfers</a> &middot;
  <a href="/adelaide-airport-to-barossa-valley-distance-and-transfer-times">All distances and
  pickup detail</a></p>
</Content>
